  {
   "text": "Saturn is raining its rings away.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 2.24
  },
  {
   "text": "It orbits nearly ten times farther from the Sun than Earth.",
   "start": 2.86,
   "end": 5.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Dark bands in its glow suggest ring rain: charged ice falling along magnetic field lines.",
   "start": 6.12,
   "end": 11.18
  },
  {
   "text": "One estimate: an Olympic pool every half hour.",
   "start": 11.86,
   "end": 14.56
  },
  {
   "text": "One model leaves under a hundred million years; a 2024 simulation says billions.",
   "start": 15.12,
   "end": 19.4
  },
  {
   "text": "A ringless Saturn is only hypothetical.",
   "start": 20.22,
